{
  "abstract": "Two explicit simple graphs on 378 vertices have equal ordinary U-polynomials and different loopy polynomials, refuting Conjecture 8.1 of Kirillov, Nenashev, Shapiro and Vaintrob (arXiv:2609.07728v2). Lean proves equality of their full finite-palette Tutte coloring sums and inequality of their two-color loopy evaluations modulo seven. The project also proves the specialization's loopy deletion–contraction rule.",
